.playwright-mcp/
_archive/
mcp-server/dist/

# Compiled Python artefacts. NOT merely noise: a .pyc keeps the SOURCE STRINGS
# in its bytecode, so a committed .pyc goes on leaking identifiers long after the
# source has been purged -- and a directory-copy distribution ships whatever sits
# in the tree. Gitignoring is not enough on its own: the file has to actually be
# absent. (Day 130: the leak guard's own .pyc was published carrying 6 client-name
# hits in its bytecode, invisible to the guard because the guard refused to open it.)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
